@startuml remote-worker-transfer
' Revision 2026-10-13: accepted architecture-review findings; no rendering or qualification claimed.
' Revision 2026-10-13: R-TRANSFER adopted round; design labels/formats unpublished, no renderer or qualification evidence.
title R-TRANSFER: code as data, then exact candidate review and board integration
actor "Orchestrator / original run requester" as O
participant "Dispatcher workspace contract\nno repository; journaled digests" as D
participant "Approved workspace executors\nchild UID; materialize / export" as E
participant "Workplace round\nzero egress; exec profile; private home" as W
participant "User manager + service-principal executor\naccount-wide absence and write fence" as U
participant "Board change-request machinery\nresource/import/candidate/verdict/integration" as B
participant "Independent trusted reviewer\nnot producer or untrusted-class" as R
participant "R-VERIFY ephemeral runners\nanother machine; no secrets" as V
participant "Donor loop\ncontinues across rework; signed letters" as L

== materialize / work ==
O -> D: admitted exact repository commit B as bounded canonical tree archive
D -> D: journal archive digest; no repository held
D -> D: plan binds immutable-B mode/content manifest, exporter/caps, repair budget and bounded cleanup consent
D -> E: swarma-workspace-materialize before work; distinct execution claim/receipt
E -> E: verify archive path/kind/mode/content against manifest; missing/extra/mismatch refuses
E -> W: standalone private Git; fresh config; no hooks/remotes/credential helpers
D -> D: plan digest covers B, canonical mode/content manifest digest, task write scope and exec profile
O -> L: signed task letter + resource attachments; resources read-only beside workspace with plan digests
L -> W: admitted tools via SSH relay; worker edits data only
note over W, L
  Worker Git/commits/history never used; no worker network/push/merge-request access.
  Validators outside write scope unless task is about them; dependencies read-only seeded caches.
  Default donor provider endpoints + our host only; no search/fetch; worker asks for resources by letter.
end note

== round end / export ==
L -> O: signed final envelope (local worker: board outcome)
O -> U: fence round and account-wide journaled stop / confirm absence
U -> W: refuse further workspace tools; no account process remains
break absence/fence unknown
  U --> O: retain cleanup obligation; no export/home deletion
end
D -> E: separately claimed exporter launch after absence; bounded cleanup consent for ordinary expiry only
note over D, E
  Distinct materialize/work/export execution evidence; lost replies reconcile, never duplicate.
  Security holds need separate authority; no launch of a retiring generation or R-SESSION reuse.
  Bounded cleanup capacity/storage accounting; caller retrieval requires current authority.
end note
E -> W: no-follow mode + content comparison with immutable manifest; pinned caps/exporter, stop at first cap excess
alt deterministic whole-export refusal (no partial result)
  E --> D: immutable refusal; no C; retained obligation
  opt separately admitted repair with current work authority and remaining plan budget
    O -> D: same-workspace repair; no cleanup-only or hold bypass
    D -> W: reopen fences only for repair; valid edits preserved
    L -> W: refusal class/path only; bounded fix-up turn
    O -> U: close write/SSH fences, stop account and confirm absence again
    D -> E: new linked execution/export effect; repeat complete export
  end
  D --> O: unresolved refusal: retain, or per-act content-confirmed operator waiver
else interrupted / unknown or infrastructure failure
  E --> D: pending/unknown under original effect; no discharge or deletion
else recorded complete export
  E --> D: changed content + executable bit, symlink text, deletion prior mode
end
note over E, D
  Four outcomes: recorded export, policy refusal, interrupted/unknown, authorized discard.
  Permission denial of known source entry needs published typed classification; infrastructure denial stays failure.
  No chmod/privilege increase. Terminal replay returns retained result; linked re-observation only.
  For the same unchanged quiesced tree, contradiction compares recorded/refused class or recorded digest,
  not walk-dependent diagnostics; this comparison does not span an admitted repair.
  Standing automatic discard is unchosen/off; expiry grants cleanup collection, never repair.
end note
break authorized discard instead of recorded export
  D --> O: journal per-act waiver; deletion may proceed; no C
  O -> O: next round may use last admitted base under new work authority
end
break export not recorded
  D --> O: retain obligation; no candidate or home deletion
end
D -> D: digest/size verify result + every blob; durable custody outside home/deletion path
break incomplete content / storage failure
  D --> O: pending obligation; metadata-only journal cannot authorize deletion
end
D -> D: journal complete-content receipt; home may retire, retained content awaits authenticated import acknowledgement or authorized release
D --> O: swarma-dispatcher workspace-result/1; producer DRAFT fields, transport/lifecycle gated; authenticated caller
O -> B: accept result as resource only
note over E, B
  RWP v2.1 sections 8/10 gates: special files, .git components however spelled,
  case-fold/Unicode-normalisation collisions, gitlinks/submodules, root escape,
  file-count/per-file/total/binary cap exceeded -> whole export refusal.
  Caps/formats unpublished. Intermediate turn-boundary export uses same fence/absence.
  Home deletion waits for recorded export or explicit operator waiver; never silently dropped.
end note

== candidate / review ==
O -> B: independently recompute canonical manifest from immutable repository B; retain admission checks
break base_commit != B or manifest_digest != recomputed digest
  B --> O: refuse before candidate (including stale rework base)
end
O -> B: deterministic import on B in scratch index; hooks off; no attribute filters/drivers
break .git component / outside write scope / .task-board change
  B --> O: hard refusal, no candidate
end
B -> B: candidate C signed by repository identity; worker/run/result-digest trailers
B -> B: C tree equals independent recomputation from B + change set
B -> R: review exactly C; flagged paths explicit hunk-by-hunk acknowledgement
R -> V: orchestrate all candidate code execution (tests/builds/generators)
V --> B: data-only results in testing state; controlled dependency egress
note over B, R
  Flagged classes: CI, Git behaviour, hooks/auto-run, agent instructions/config, all symlinks.
  Exact path list: CIP-0009 D5a. No pre-acceptance untrusted candidate push to CI with secrets.
  K1 acceptance binds C, never transferred by patch equality.
end note

alt changes requested
  R -> B: findings bound to C
  O -> L: signed rework task letter: findings + admitted base C
  D -> E: materialize afresh from C; prior deletion requires complete-content custody or explicit waiver
  E -> W: next round; export yields C2 on C; same gates/review
else accepted
  R -> B: exact C verdict
  O -> B: request integration of accepted exact head
  break base moved
    B --> O: ordinary base refresh + re-review
  end
  B -> B: signed fast-forward accepted exact head (K1/K3)
end
note over D, V
  Materialize/export: dispatcher workspace owner, approved child-UID executors.
  Import/candidate/review/integration: board change-request owner, orchestrator executes.
  Result DRAFT fields are producer-published; archive/plan/transport/lifecycle/trailer/verdict/runner formats gated.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D5a-D5d]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#publication-status Publication register]]
end note
@enduml
